---
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import chrisPhoto from '../assets/team/chris-mcleod.jpg';
import alexPhoto from '../assets/team/alex-maclean.jpg';
---

<Base
  title="About — BluHeron Interactive"
  description="BluHeron Interactive is a creative technology studio in London and Hamilton, Ontario, designing and producing immersive public artwork and digital tools for the arts sector."
>
  <section class="wrap head">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1 class="display">We design, build, and deliver the work <em class="clay">ourselves</em>.</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap story">
    <p>
      BluHeron Interactive is a creative technology studio based in London and Hamilton,
      Ontario. We design and produce immersive and interactive public artwork, and we build
      the software that supports it. Our work has been commissioned by municipalities, arts
      councils, galleries, festivals, and community organizations across Ontario, and has been
      installed in galleries, market squares, sculpture gardens, a landfill site, and the
      middle of a street festival.
    </p>
    <p>
      The studio brings together a long practice in community-engaged public art and a
      background in immersive media and software development. That range sits inside a single
      small team rather than across a chain of contractors, which means the people who design
      a project are the people who build it and the people on site when it opens.
    </p>
    <p>
      The structure is deliberate. We are not a design consultancy that hands over a concept,
      and not a development shop waiting for a specification. Because one team carries a
      commission from proposal to closing night, the work is scoped against real conditions —
      weather, crowds, accessibility requirements, and public budgets — from the first sketch.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band now">
    <div class="wrap inner">
      <p class="kicker">Current work</p>
      <p class="now-lede">
        <a href={withBase('/beacbeac/')}>beacbeac</a>, our platform for accessible,
        place-based stories, is deployed this fall at Ability First Fest and Supercrawl in
        Hamilton and at Nuit Blanche London. The studio is a business member of the Canadian
        Museums Association, provides web development and hosting for the Mississauga Arts
        Council, and has delivered development work for Centre[4]Arts.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap principles">
    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <div class="grid stagger">
      <article class="principle reveal">
        <h3>Co-creation over consultation</h3>
        <p>
          Participation is the artwork, not a survey attached to one.{' '}
          <a href={withBase('/work/navitas/')}>Navitas</a> required two people pumping in
          tandem to move water across Hamilton.{' '}
          <a href={withBase('/work/jump-around/')}>Jump Around</a> carried the City of
          Hamilton's public art consultation inside a game show and returned the results to
          the department.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle reveal">
        <h3>Accessibility as a starting condition</h3>
        <p>
          beacbeac was co-designed with Blind, Low Vision, Deaf, Deafblind, and disabled
          community members. Access requirements shape the brief rather than a remediation
          pass at the end of it.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle reveal">
        <h3>Work with what is already there</h3>
        <p>
          Navitas threads 2,000 LEDs through reclaimed copper, aluminum, and wood. The{' '}
          <a href={withBase('/work/landfill-education-model/')}>Landfill Education Model</a>{' '}
          makes a working municipal system legible to the people who fund it. Existing
          materials and existing infrastructure are the starting point.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle reveal">
        <h3>Committed to the arts sector</h3>
        <p>
          Our digital services — websites, hosting, maintenance, and accessibility audits —
          are offered to arts councils, galleries, studios, and festivals. Staying inside the
          sector keeps the studio close to the organizations our public work is made with.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap team">
    <h2>Our team</h2>
    <div class="people">
      <article class="person reveal">
        <Image src={chrisPhoto} alt="Portrait of Christopher McLeod" width={600} widths={[300, 600]} sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 300px" />
        <h3>Christopher McLeod</h3>
        <p class="role">Co-founder &middot; Artistic director</p>
        <p>
          A freelance artist and artistic director for three decades, Chris has led 24
          community-engaged public art projects across Ontario. He holds a BA in Studio Art
          from McMaster University and an MFA from Emily Carr University of Art + Design,
          where his research focused on social practice and community interaction. His
          practice centres on creating opportunities for people to connect meaningfully, with
          the artwork emerging from those encounters.
        </p>
        <p class="land">
          Chris is of settler ancestry, living on the traditional territory of the
          Haudenosaunee, Wendat, and Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="person reveal">
        <Image src={alexPhoto} alt="Portrait of Alex MacLean" width={600} widths={[300, 600]} sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 300px" />
        <h3>Alex MacLean</h3>
        <p class="role">Co-founder &middot; Artist &amp; creative technologist</p>
        <p>
          An immersive media artist and developer, Alex art-directs and builds — from
          generative audiovisual installations such as{' '}
          <a href={withBase('/work/blue-noise/')}>Blue Noise</a> and{' '}
          <a href={withBase('/work/concrete-canopy/')}>Concrete Canopy</a> to the beacbeac
          platform, its apps and administration console, and the websites the studio maintains
          for arts organizations.
        </p>
        <p class="land">
          <a href="https://alexmaclean.ca" rel="noopener">alexmaclean.ca &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactCTA heading="New commissions, partnerships &amp; collaborations — <em>let’s talk</em>." />
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px) clamp(24px, 4vw, 36px);
  }

  .head em.clay {
    color: var(--clay);
  }

  .story {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 22px;
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 7vw, 72px);
  }

  .story p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .now .inner {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 72px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .now-lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .principles {
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 88px) clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  .principles h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  /* Four principles read as a balanced 2x2 rather than a row of three with
     an orphan trailing underneath it. */
  .principles .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .principles .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .principle {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 22px;
  }

  .principle h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .principle p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .team {
    padding-block: 0 clamp(56px, 8vw, 88px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  .team h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .people {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
  }

  .person {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .person img {
    width: min(300px, 100%);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .person h3 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  .role {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--clay);
  }

  .person p:not(.role) {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .person .land {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

</style>
